      "text": "To start, we will find the semiperimeter of the triangle:\n$$\\frac{7 + 8 + 9}{2} = \\frac{24}{2} = 12$$\nLet $a$, $b$, and $c$ be the side lengths of the triangle.  Then, we have\n$$a = 7, b = 8, c = 9$$\nWe will extend the interior triangle bisectors of each side.\nWe can see that the red line bisecting the perimeter of the triangle will\nintersect at a point at some unknown distance from the vertices of the triangle.\nSo we will approximate the intersection point of the red line with this point\nas the midpoint of the unknown distance.  Let $p$ be this unknown distance.\nThen, the point $P$ is (A + p)/2 and (7 + p)/2.  Let A' be the midpoint of b and A + p.\nThen, we know that $\\frac{7 + p}{2} \\in A'$.  Let $A$ have the coordinates\n(-0.5, 0), $A'$ be (3, 0), and P be (-0.5 + p/2, $p/2$).\nTherefore, the slope of $RP$ is\n$$m_1 = \\frac{p/2 - 0}{(-0.5 + p/2) - 3} = m_2 = \\frac{p/2}{(p - 6.5)/2}$$\nThen, the equation of the line $RP$ will be\n$$y = p/2 \\frac{x - 3}{p - 6.5} \\tag{1}$$\nWe can find the unknown point $R$ in a similar manner.  Let $p$ be again\nthe unknown distance.  Then, recall that B is at (8, 0), and\nthe angle at degree $90$ of the red line is approximately\n$30$ degrees. Therefore, we solve the equation\n$$\\tan(30) = \\frac{p}{8 - p}$$\nThen, we combine the equations of the two lines to form a quadratic in $p$.\nSolving the critical points we get $8.280596302$, but by process of elimination\n$$p \\in (3.269381655, 6.452279537) $$\nSo, we have approximately $(6.452279537 - 3.269381655)/6.452279537 = 0.5537435148573145$.\nWe can find the slope of this line to be $m_1 = \\frac{p}{9 - (6.452279537 - 3.269381655)} = \\frac{p}{9.389998457}$.\nAnyway, it is simple to see that $\\tan(\\theta) = \\frac{\\frac{p}{9 - (6.452279537 - 3.269381655)}}{((6.452279537 - 3.269381655)! + 9)} \\approx 0.186459768886747$.\nSo, $\\tan(\\theta) = \\boxed{0.1865}$.\n\n[asy]\nunitsize(0.075 cm);\n\npair A, B, C, P, R, Q, X;\n\nB = (8,0);\nC = (8,0);\nA = dir(-135);\nP = (12/7,B) + ( (19/7)*dir(293.5)); C = (C + P)/2;\nR = (9/6,C) + ( (11/6)*dir(224)); P = (P + R)/2;\nQ = (abs((C + C))/2,P);\nX = (intersectionpoint(B--C,P--Q));\ndraw(A--B--C--cycle);\ndraw(interp(P,Q,X,-0.2)--interp(P,Q,X,1.2),red); draw(interp(R,S,X,-0.2)--interp(R,S,X,1.2),blue);\nlabel(\"$\\theta$\", X + (0.8,0.4)); label(\"$A$\", A, E, dir(315));\nlabel(\"$B$\", B, NE, sqrt(3)/2); label(\"$C$\", C, NE, sqrt(3)/2);\nlabel(\"$P$\", P, N, dir(85));\nlabel(\"$Q$\", Q, E, dir(90));\nlabel(\"$R$\", R, W, dir(125));\n[/asy]\nWait, they're both 75 degrees O____O\nForgot that tac..",
